    <exercise number="41" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Prove that $$\log_{b}(n) = \frac{1}{\log_{n}(b)}$$ for any positive integers $$b &gt; 1$$ and $$n &gt; 1.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Let $$b b$$ and $$n n$$ be positive integers greater than $$1. 1.$$ Then, by the change-of-base formula, $$log b ( n )= log n ( n ) log n ( b ) = 1 log n ( b ) . log b ( n )= log n ( n ) log n ( b ) = 1 log n ( b ) .$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
